# Full Stack Floor Map (Floors)

Extension for `@luizsantiago/fullstack-floor-map`. Requires Spec Seatbelt (`agent-architecture.md`).

## Layer registry (Floors)

Read `.specs/project/PROJECT.md` § **Layer registry** before each Execute task. One layer skill per turn: **frontend**, **backend**, **data**, **analytics**, **datascience**.

| Task `Files` vs registry | Load | Do not load |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Matches **one** layer | That `*-engineering.md` | Other layer skills |
| Matches **zero** layers | Neither — `engineering-standards.md` only | Layer skills |
| Matches **two or more** | **STOP** — split task | All layer skills |

Always keep Seatbelt `engineering-standards.md` + `references/implement.md`. Layer skills are additive.

## Specialist catalog (optional depth)

After the layer manual is chosen, you may load **at most one** catalog skill (`…/SKILL.md` under `.cursor/skills/<id>/`) whose `metadata.domain` matches that layer. Open **at most two** `references/` files for the current topic. Prefer § Stack in `PROJECT.md` when several specialists match.

Specialists do not override task `Gate` or `PROJECT.md` test commands. Discover APIs from the repo.

## Pairing with Spec Seatbelt

Vertical **feature**, horizontal **tasks** — one Floor per `Files`. Run `npx @luizsantiago/fullstack-floor-map validate-layers <feature>` (same as `python3 .specs/seatbelt/scripts/validate_layer_routing.py`).

## After commit / Verify

Drop layer + specialist before the next task. On **/verify**, load **no** Floors layers and **no** catalog specialists — use Seatbelt Verify only (`validate.md`, `security-review.md`, then at most one of `appsec.md` or `qa-strategy.md`).

## Re-install

Seatbelt `install` does not delete Floors skills. Re-run `npx @luizsantiago/fullstack-floor-map install` to refresh layers, rule, layer gate, and catalog.
